harles in every published poll since summer, with margins ranging from about eight to thirteen points and an average near eleven. Independent Rick Bennett is on the ballot but has trailed well back and raised far less than either major-party nominee.\n\nRaters across the spectrum call the race Solid or Likely Democratic, and prediction markets put Democratic win odds in the mid-nineties. Pingree has out-raised Charles roughly two to one and holds a cash advantage, while Senator Angus King's endorsement adds establishment backing. The main uncertainty is turnout in a midterm featuring a competitive Senate race atop Maine's ticket, but both the polling and the money point to a Democratic hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9757, "margin": 10.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9716, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9705, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9685, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9649, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9585, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.96, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9621, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.961, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9719, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9653, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9728, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9678, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9699, "margin": 11.0}]}